================================================================================================
STEP 1.  Delta^(3)_r(t,b,h) has vanishing h^0, h^1 AND h^2 coefficients
         (h^0 = Fact 2, h^1 = Fact 3, h^2 = the NEW H_r ODE).
================================================================================================
   r=0..24, b=0..4 : all three brackets vanish identically in t : True
   => Delta^(3)_r = sum_{k>=3} h^k q^(3)_k(t,b),  hence |Delta^(3)_r| <= A3_r(b) h^3
      uniformly on t in [0,1], by the SS4 coefficient-sum lemma, unchanged.

