================================================================================================
STEP 4.  Consequence: n^2 R_r(m,b,n) -> H_r(t,b) uniformly, with an explicit rate
         | n^2 R_r(m,b,n) - H_r(t,b) | <= D3_r(b)/n .
         So limsup_n max_m n^2|R_r| = max_{t in [0,1]}|H_r(t,b)| = H_r(1,b) =: D*_r(b),
         since every coefficient of H_r(.,b) is > 0 (closed form) and the grid
         {m/n} becomes dense in [0,1].
================================================================================================
   r=3 b=0 : D*_r(b) = 5/28           = 0.178571429 ;  rate constant D3_r(b) = 0.257143
   r=4 b=0 : D*_r(b) = 103/315        = 0.326984127 ;  rate constant D3_r(b) = 2.00292
